    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0687" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4453: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-14T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1923—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 14—9:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>399. My 397, December 11, 5 p.m. Senior consul at Canton telegraphs he will
                    deliver communication to Sun today.</p>
                <p>American consul general, Canton, telegraphs December 13, 6 p.m.: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Conditions are quiet but tense. Commander of South China Patrol ordering
                            four destroyers to arrive Canton Saturday. General opinion of consular
                            body Sun will not act before Monday.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>This looks as though Jenkins expected Sun to take some step before the expiration
                    of two weeks’ delay. See my 389, December 8, 10 a.m., and 392 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">391</hi>], December 9, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>Four destroyers mentioned are part of a force of six destroyers which commander
                    in chief United States Asiatic Fleet despatched from Manila December 11th, and
                    which arrived in Hongkong December 15th [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]. They
                    have landing force of marines on board. Please reply by telegraph to my 394,
                    December 11, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="83" xml:id="d424-f1"/> last paragraph.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
